    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nRefurbished 3 bedroom Bungalow of c. 95 sqm on c. 1 acre with outbuildings. 7 km from Longford Town Centre an just 3 km off the N4 Dublin Road.\n\nIn the last 3 years the house was replumbed and rewired along with a new Kitchen and Bathroom and a contemporary décor throughout.\n\nThe house features a spacious bright living area with a solid fuel stove (with back boiler) and polished porcelain tiled floors, there is a dual aspect to the east and west with double glass doors opening onto the rear of the house that is a real sun trap.\n\nOff the living area the kitchen has the same tiled floor and substantial built in units with integrated appliances , under cabinet lighting and a double electric range oven. Off the kitchen is one of the bedrooms that could also be used as a home office taking advantage of the fibre to the home broadband available.\n\nThere are two double sized bedrooms, the main bedroom is very spacious. The family bathroom is fully tiled with a separate shower contemporary fittings and a heated towel rail.\n\nThe house comes with an inventory of furniture included.\n\n\nServices:\n• Mains Water and Septic tank, \n• Dual System Central Heating (oil boiler & Solid fuel stove)\n• Fibre to the home broadband available.\n\n\nOutside:\nThe house is on a large site of just over an acre. There is a large stone yard to the side and rear of the house where there a workshop and shed.\n\nThere is a large concrete base in place that would be suitable for another shed or mobile home / studio.\n\nBehind this is a paddock.\n\n\nLocation: \nThe house is situated beside the Carriglass estate demesne and looks out over the mature woods.\n\nThe area is quiet and rural yet is just 3km from N4 Dublin Sligo Road and 7km (10 mins drive) from Longford Town center.\n\n\nEircode: N39 CA48 \n\nGPS: 53.7318, -7.7152"
      },
